# The CA certificates the server's certificate has to chain to: Amazon Trust
# Services' RSA roots, 1 and 2, which Kii Cloud's certificates chain to, and
# Starfield Services' G2, for PolarSSL. Kii Cloud's server sends Root CA 1
# cross-signed by Starfield's root: mbedTLS takes Root CA 1, which it has, for
# the chain's end, and PolarSSL 1.3 goes on up the chain the server sends, to
# Starfield's root, which it has to have too. Not Amazon's ECC roots, 3 and
# 4: the SDK builds mbedTLS without ECDSA, which can't read them, and ebisu's
# mbedTLS port takes the certificates only if it reads them all; and
# PolarSSL, which reads them, without ECDSA too, which couldn't check a chain
# to them. Replace them with those of the server the device connects to, or
# set EBISU_SAMPLE_CA_FILE.

